WEBVTT

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:32.460
These guys play the best tunes!

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:35.260
Listening to pirate radio again, lo?

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:37.390
At least wear headphones.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:39.720
You gotta feel the music
in your bones.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:42.810
- Isn't this an old broadcast?
- I like this one.

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:45.770
You definitely picked up the signal
at the perfect time.

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:48.060
Maybe the thunderbolts
are bringing it to us.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:51.440
- Or the Minovsky particles are--
- Thin? Whatever.

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:53.740
- Make me a copy later.
- Right here!

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:56.820
This part is perfect to listen to
before a mission!

00:01:56.990 --> 00:01:58.990
I know how you feel.

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:01.410
I can see it now.

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:04.000
Me, flying through the debris,
dodging at the last second.

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:11.670
The vibrations tell me what my hands
and feet should do with the controls.

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:27.020
Everything acts as my eyes as they move.

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:33.150
Can't they do something about
this nasty air in the hangar?

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:36.280
- It's just your sinuses again.
- Cornelius, gimme some tissues.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.360
You better return 'em.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.870
- Thanks.
- Later!

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:46.950
<i>Here is your mission objective.</i>

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:49.540
<i>You are to eliminate
the snipers that are hiding</i>

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:51.670
<i>in our home of Side 4, Moore.</i>

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:56.090
<i>In the past month, over 40 friendlies
have been shot down.</i>

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.880
<i>We must never forgive the cowardly
enemy who destroyed our home,</i>

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:01.720
<i>the Thunderbolt Sector.</i>

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:05.520
<i>This war is reaching
its final stages,</i>

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:07.680
<i>and retaking this sector</i>

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:10.400
<i>will play a pivotal role in its outcome.</i>

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:13.560
<i>Renewed prosperity to Side 4, Moore!</i>

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:15.860
<i>Death to the cowardly Zeon!</i>

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:18.570
Preaching to the brotherhood, huh?

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:22.870
Man, my birthplace
refuses to let me go.

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:42.720
Free jazz is perfect
for the Thunderbolt.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:49.270
I love mobile suits.
And space and the battlefield.

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:50.850
Because I'm free out here.

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:00.900
Oh, crap! They can see
exactly where we are!

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:03.870
If they open fire, we'll just trace
it back to pinpoint their location.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:11.620
Now, who's gonna draw the short straw?

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:21.130
<i>- Who was hit?!
- Ensign lo!</i>

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:28.140
Commander! Command--

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:31.560
Break-break! Commander Allen
hit by beam cannon!

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:33.600
Suit completely destroyed!

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:35.560
Enemy is sniping from behind the debris!

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:38.980
Radio comms will never reach with
the Minovsky particle density this high!

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:40.650
Just focus on the enemy--

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:42.780
Dave!

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:46.120
Locate those enemy snipers!

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.410
How can they see us?!

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:50.660
The Minovsky particles are too dense!

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:53.330
- Calculate their location, damn it!
- It's Side 4!

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:56.000
Are you telling us to
attack our own home?!

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:21.440
Barrel has exceeded lifespan.

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:24.360
This is Daryl, now switching to
trajectory prediction relay role.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:27.870
<i>Good job, CPO Daryl.
I'll take it from here.</i>

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:30.660
This'll make me a shoo-in
for the Zeon Cross!

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:34.870
To brag to your girl back home?
Or to...

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:38.500
Sean, Ensign Hoover's reporting
situation is complicated.

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:44.340
<i>Lay off! I'm gonna bag 'em real soon!
Both these Feds and all the girls!</i>

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:53.520
Damn, Daryl's good.
Is he clairvoyant or something?

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:55.810
Or maybe he's one of those Newtypes.

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:58.860
I'm gonna get an award back home
and then go on R&R!

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:09.570
Ensign Hoover, is your suit drifting?
Your comms are breaking up.

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:11.910
<i>Please check your cable connection.</i>

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:14.080
They are?

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.330
Huh?

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:23.880
Hey!

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:26.720
<i>Hoover!</i>

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:29.760
<i>It's a person!
That's a Fed normal suit'!</i>

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:33.100
<i>Daryl! Do you have a shot?!
I don't have one from my position!</i>

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:34.600
<i>But Hoover might be--</i>

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:37.390
<i>He was shot in the head!
You saw him!</i>

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:52.950
The cockpit's not too different
from a Zaku's.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:58.500
Yo. You look like the ace
of this sniper unit,

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:00.210
but you have mediocre
taste in music.

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:01.880
I'm disappointed.

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:04.210
Big talk, coming from someone
who only caught a lucky break.

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:06.460
<i>And sneaking around,
shooting people from far away</i>

00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:08.720
<i>is the perfect job for folks
with peg legs.</i>

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:12.760
Are you laughing at my legs?

00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:15.390
I have your firing positions.

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:17.480
I just need to pick a blind spot
and stroll home.

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:22.400
You're not getting away next time.
Mark my words, I'll take you down.

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:26.980
I'm Chief Petty Officer Daryl Lorenz.
And I'll always be gunning for you.

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:29.950
The name's Ensign lo Fleming.

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:33.160
When you hear jazz,
that's your cue that I'm on the stage.

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:20.200
Patty Page, right?
That was "Tennessee Waltz".

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:23.710
- Oh, you heard this?
- I'm a Royal Teens fan, myself.

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:25.380
For "Short Shorts"?

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:27.500
<i>No, for this.</i>

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:28.710
Ah.

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:31.220
Let me know if you
want to borrow it.

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:32.720
Maybe later.

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:41.640
24 went out,
and this is all that came back?

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:45.060
That's what happens with
ops thought up by that bitch.

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:04.420
Move it to the maintenance hangar!
Top priority!

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:09.750
Lo!

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:18.890
Ensign lo Fleming has returned.

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:34.860
I never did like this guy.
He was such a playboy-wannabe.

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:40.700
Take the body to the Reuse Lab.

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:44.370
It was a miracle that we found him.
We want to return him to his family.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:47.040
Retrieving the data from
his prosthetic arm comes first.

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:49.130
You're treating him like a lab rat
even after he's dead?

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:52.460
You're all able to fight
thanks to that data, remember?

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:55.130
Prof. Karla?
They're taking the body to...

00:09:57.550 --> 00:09:58.220
Professor?

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:07.650
No!

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:10.150
No...

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:21.160
<i>Heavy damage, 4.
Light damage, 6.</i>

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:23.660
<i>Cockpit block only, 5.
Lost, 9.</i>

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:25.660
Understood...

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:32.670
We're currently extracting data from
the Rick Dom that Ensign lo Fleming stole.

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:36.170
It might let us predict the enemy's
deployment and movement patterns.

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:37.170
Fine.

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:41.550
Also, the item is currently being
loaded into a container.

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:44.560
The mechanics we dispatched
are coming back with it,

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:47.140
so I'm told we can begin
startup tests right away.

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:48.850
Who do we assign it to?

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:51.270
I believe Ensign lo is the only choice.

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:52.860
True...

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:55.190
Shall I give him the order?

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:58.200
No, I'll tell him.

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:15.550
A prototype mobile suit?

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:18.340
Did the Moore Brotherhood
front some money to the Federation?

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:23.550
Everyone who outranked you
died in this last operation.

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:24.560
Otherwise, you...

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:28.390
We both got where we are
by our superiors dying.

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:30.060
Isn't that right, Acting Captain?

00:11:41.280 --> 00:11:44.240
Let go of my hand,
Ensign lo Fleming!

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:46.540
That's an order
from your captain.

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:48.250
Yes, sir.

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:55.090
So that's how it is...

00:11:55.210 --> 00:11:57.380
You never can tell, right?

00:11:58.090 --> 00:11:59.260
Where's the Captain?

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:02.340
The young lady is spending
quality time with her man.

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:06.680
She's captain because she's an elite.
The privileged class get all the breaks.

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:09.430
Speaking of whom, what's this about
the prototype going to lo?

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:12.350
Same with him. He's the son
of Moore's old leader.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:17.440
The incompetent elite let Zeon
invade and destroy our home.

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:21.030
Still, they're the perfect people
to offer up as sacrifices.

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:24.870
The young heroes who lay down
their lives for our ideals.

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:30.870
We'll use those with a guilty pedigree
as Moore Brotherhood propaganda.

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:33.620
That's what this Gundam is for.

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:38.750
I have to stop loving you!

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:41.300
Then I'll be able to
order you to your death.

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:45.800
Go ahead, Claudia.
Order me into battle.

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:47.550
I've been possessed.

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:52.810
By the demons called mobile suits
that shine on the battlefield.

00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:08.330
I listened to the comm logs
from the battle.

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:12.000
That Federation pilot
who killed Hoover...

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:15.460
When you hear jazz,
that's your signal that he's come, right?

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:16.960
Yes.

00:13:18.670 --> 00:13:23.260
I'm begging you, Daryl.
Make sure that you kill that man.

00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:27.680
You're our ace sniper.
You can do it, right?

00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:42.990
Prof. Karla. Can I get
some painkillers?

00:13:43.490 --> 00:13:45.360
These legs you gave me

00:13:46.530 --> 00:13:48.950
are hurting really badly tonight.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:57.960
You're checking the sniper rotation
intel from the Rick Dom!

00:13:58.040 --> 00:14:01.840
You get that, right? You just need to do
that as part of the test flight.

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:05.800
Cornelius, gimme some tissues.

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:07.220
Here you go.

00:14:07.340 --> 00:14:10.220
- And gimme some tunes, partner.
- Will do.

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:20.020
Oh, wow...

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:25.070
It's like night and day.
This... is a Gundam!

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:50.680
This is the best!
This power is exactly what I wanted!

00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:58.600
Gundam...

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:01.110
Give me your strength!

00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:08.900
It dodged me?

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:10.200
No way!

00:15:13.080 --> 00:15:15.790
Crap! What the hell?!

00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:44.150
It's jazz.

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:46.820
Three Zakus were shot down.

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:49.860
Each one's Big Gun fire was evaded.

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:53.320
This is a heavily armored and highly
maneuverable mobile suit.

00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:59.080
This is exactly what the Living Dead
Division is least equipped to handle.

00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:03.330
That's the Federation's...

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:04.040
Gundam!

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:12.260
It's him!

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:27.670
Isn't this that song your dad liked?

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:30.340
It's a sappy song.

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:33.550
You think so? I liked it.

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:36.510
Cornelius. Gimme some tissues.

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:39.430
Sure.

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:44.230
<i>Gathered here at
the space fortress A Baoa Qu</i>

00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:47.900
<i>are young, elite troops
who have performed amazing feats,</i>

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:50.440
<i>as well the leading minds
of the Principality</i>

00:17:50.730 --> 00:17:53.780
<i>who were awarded
the glorious Zeon Science Medal.</i>

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:57.030
<i>Their loyalty was praised
at the staff meeting</i>

00:17:57.110 --> 00:18:00.370
<i>of the prestigious
Zeon Space Strike Fleet!</i>

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:05.250
<i>We members of the Zeon armed forces
must become the cornerstone</i>

00:18:05.330 --> 00:18:07.750
<i>of the realization of
Spacenoid ideals!</i>

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:19.220
There's no itching
in your mind, is there?

00:18:19.300 --> 00:18:20.600
It's fine.

00:18:21.640 --> 00:18:22.600
Okay, then.

00:18:27.140 --> 00:18:29.020
Beginning recording.

00:18:32.770 --> 00:18:35.030
<i>We'll be starting
Phase 6 today.</i>

00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:36.280
I heard.

00:18:36.360 --> 00:18:37.900
<i>We need to run
checks first, right?</i>

00:18:38.030 --> 00:18:39.950
Yes, of course.

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:42.160
Neural transmission shows green.

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:46.410
<i>Step off with your right foot.
Now pull it back, and then...</i>

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:48.580
Good! Now your left.

00:18:48.670 --> 00:18:53.300
Switch from right to left in time
with the speed on the bar.

00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:56.170
Okay! Professor!

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:59.680
Begin Reuse Psycho Device
operation test.

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:01.600
Roger that.

00:20:40.650 --> 00:20:45.450
It's an amazing system.
I bet it'll let us act as more than snipers.

00:20:46.160 --> 00:20:49.790
We have far better
artificial legs than those.

00:20:50.620 --> 00:20:52.210
I know.

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:56.130
But that system will let me do more than
I ever could with my real legs, right?

00:20:56.750 --> 00:20:58.590
You want another medal?

00:20:58.670 --> 00:21:01.260
You got one, too!

00:21:01.380 --> 00:21:04.680
I threw it away.
I hate war.

00:21:31.660 --> 00:21:35.330
Gundam! Let's see you
blow my mind!

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:42.960
<i>Noise level nominal.
All green.</i>

00:21:43.130 --> 00:21:43.800
Thanks.

00:21:44.970 --> 00:21:49.010
<i>Chief Daryl, you don't think
this place is haunted, do you?</i>

00:21:49.140 --> 00:21:50.010
Out in space?

00:21:50.180 --> 00:21:55.600
<i>Lots of people died at Side 4,
so I was wondering if sensitives see ghosts here.</i>

00:21:55.690 --> 00:21:57.600
<i>Horror movies freak me out,
so I just thought...</i>

00:21:57.690 --> 00:21:58.860
Well, I don't see any.

00:21:58.980 --> 00:22:01.020
<i>Oh, really? That's a relief...</i>

00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:02.320
<i>Ah.</i>

00:22:02.440 --> 00:22:05.990
<i>It's terrible, you having to
go out in a Zaku I, Chief.</i>

00:22:06.150 --> 00:22:08.530
<i>Even if this is all we have left,</i>

00:22:08.570 --> 00:22:10.780
<i>our ace sniper deserves better
than some ancient Zaku I.</i>

00:22:10.870 --> 00:22:13.450
A sniper doesn't need mobility.

00:22:13.660 --> 00:22:16.830
I'll just shoot any prey that gets
caught in our net, same as always.

00:22:16.920 --> 00:22:18.460
This is plenty.

00:22:19.710 --> 00:22:23.670
<i>I figured you'd say that.
I hope you avenge our friends.</i>

00:22:23.800 --> 00:22:25.380
<i>Well, good hunting.</i>

00:22:25.800 --> 00:22:27.220
Thanks.

00:22:41.730 --> 00:22:44.070
<i>Fisher! Sean!
He's in your area!</i>

00:22:45.240 --> 00:22:46.400
Gotcha!

00:22:47.570 --> 00:22:49.570
He's fast!
Try this, then!

00:22:55.000 --> 00:22:56.410
Over there, huh?

00:23:00.630 --> 00:23:01.750
Crap!

00:23:08.470 --> 00:23:10.090
You're mine!

00:23:13.390 --> 00:23:15.020
Damn it...

00:23:18.560 --> 00:23:19.560
Sean!

00:23:21.310 --> 00:23:23.730
Bunch of cowardly snakes!

00:23:23.820 --> 00:23:28.570
Can't you fight outside of your
hidey-holes in this debris?!

00:23:29.110 --> 00:23:30.860
Hit, damn it!

00:23:33.990 --> 00:23:35.910
That was too small!
Fisher, that blast...

00:23:36.290 --> 00:23:37.330
wasn't the Gundam!

00:23:38.160 --> 00:23:40.580
Where are you?
Where did you hide,

00:23:40.710 --> 00:23:42.130
Gundam?!

00:23:46.920 --> 00:23:49.630
That was also too small!
Was it another decoy?

00:23:57.850 --> 00:24:00.390
Move! Move, damn it!

00:24:04.440 --> 00:24:05.820
Now to finish you off!

00:24:10.360 --> 00:24:11.490
I see you!

00:24:32.130 --> 00:24:36.350
That's one hell of a long shot...
Sniping me at this range

00:24:36.470 --> 00:24:39.930
means that it's you,
isn't it, Peglegs?

00:24:40.390 --> 00:24:44.270
A thunderbolt deflected the beam?!
I can't believe this guy's luck!

00:24:44.560 --> 00:24:48.940
Run, Daryl! When a sniper's location
is given away, he's history!

00:24:49.070 --> 00:24:51.400
You're no match for a Gundam!

00:24:51.490 --> 00:24:54.450
Crap! I can't see a thing!

00:24:57.830 --> 00:25:00.330
Sean! He's still alive?!

00:25:00.540 --> 00:25:03.620
If you can predict my movements,
I dare you to fire!

00:25:03.750 --> 00:25:06.210
If you're prepared to kill
one of your own, that is!

00:25:06.330 --> 00:25:09.130
Shoot! Shoot this guy, Daryl!

00:25:15.470 --> 00:25:17.430
Trying to create a distraction
by adding to the debris, huh?

00:25:17.510 --> 00:25:21.520
I'll make a path for you. Come closer!
I'll put a shot through just you!

00:25:25.980 --> 00:25:28.060
This song has me so pumped up!

00:25:28.150 --> 00:25:31.070
When you hear jazz like this,
it's all over for you!

00:25:35.820 --> 00:25:38.990
- What the--?
- Light up!

00:25:45.040 --> 00:25:46.420
Sean!

00:25:51.670 --> 00:25:53.010
Above me?!

00:26:03.390 --> 00:26:06.600
With that body of yours,
that must be the best you can do!

00:26:06.690 --> 00:26:07.810
Bastard!

00:26:08.020 --> 00:26:10.610
It's over, Peglegs!

00:26:22.540 --> 00:26:24.200
You son of a--

00:26:56.950 --> 00:26:59.280
Focus attack on the center
of the enemy fleet!

00:26:59.360 --> 00:27:00.660
Maintain speed!

00:27:00.740 --> 00:27:03.660
Keep shooting until we're
out of firing range!

00:27:07.710 --> 00:27:11.460
- Two Musais destroyed!
- Ten seconds to edge of firing range!

00:27:17.260 --> 00:27:20.510
We sank two Musais
with a single decoy Gundam.

00:27:20.640 --> 00:27:23.010
A fine plan, Captain.

00:27:23.100 --> 00:27:25.470
That's all we managed...?

00:27:27.640 --> 00:27:30.690
Running away again, huh?

00:28:10.020 --> 00:28:12.900
I'll dig up a new prosthetic hand for you.
Give me a minute.

00:28:37.960 --> 00:28:42.260
Two hours of stopgap repairs will let us
send four mobile suits back into action.

00:28:42.680 --> 00:28:45.550
Only one Big Gun remains.

00:28:46.100 --> 00:28:48.930
Your team should be prepared
to die rather than surrender.

00:28:49.100 --> 00:28:52.770
The division has been ordered to defend
this sector to the death.

00:28:52.850 --> 00:28:56.610
If need be, the science team
is to die with us.

00:29:00.070 --> 00:29:01.030
Captain,

00:29:01.440 --> 00:29:05.370
our experiments have reached the stage
where it can be sent into the field.

00:29:05.450 --> 00:29:07.580
But that suit needs...

00:29:07.910 --> 00:29:13.120
If you mean the final key component,
I'm sure you only need to give the word.

00:29:28.850 --> 00:29:30.890
You have to understand,
Prof. Karla!

00:29:30.970 --> 00:29:34.730
This is the only way to save the division
from utter annihilation!

00:29:34.810 --> 00:29:38.480
Our experimental unit is the only thing
that can fight that Gundam!

00:29:38.610 --> 00:29:39.980
We can't, Sexton!

00:29:40.110 --> 00:29:44.700
It has to be hooked up to the nerves from
four limbs to reach its full potential!

00:29:44.780 --> 00:29:46.660
We have Chief Petty Officer Daryl.

00:29:47.820 --> 00:29:50.490
He just lost his left hand
in battle, didn't he?

00:29:50.660 --> 00:29:52.660
What are you suggesting?

00:29:53.120 --> 00:29:55.080
Cut off his right hand!

00:29:55.160 --> 00:29:56.830
They aren't lab rats!

00:29:57.000 --> 00:29:58.040
This is hard for me, too!

00:29:58.290 --> 00:30:02.840
How much more of my soul are you
going to force me to give up?!

00:30:06.340 --> 00:30:08.340
If you don't help fight this war,

00:30:08.430 --> 00:30:12.020
what will happen to your father,
who's in prison for treason?

00:30:14.350 --> 00:30:17.730
Now is the time to put your brilliant
research to work for the homeland!

00:30:17.810 --> 00:30:20.360
It's for the independence
of space emigrants!

00:30:20.480 --> 00:30:22.860
And for the Principality of Zeon!

00:32:13.090 --> 00:32:17.390
This is the real power of
the Reuse Psycho Device!

00:32:17.470 --> 00:32:19.230
I can crush the Gundam with this!

00:32:29.070 --> 00:32:30.650
<i>Attention, deck crew.</i>

00:32:30.860 --> 00:32:34.280
<i>Deck 3 and 4's hatches will be open
for landing operations.</i>

00:32:34.370 --> 00:32:38.080
<i>Don helmets immediately
or move to an airtight area.</i>

00:32:38.370 --> 00:32:40.160
<i>Message from Moore Brotherhood:</i>

00:32:40.290 --> 00:32:44.290
<i>Begin all-out assault to retake
Thunderbolt Sector in two hours.</i>

00:32:44.380 --> 00:32:45.630
<i>Message ends.</i>

00:32:45.920 --> 00:32:48.250
<i>Guncannons, 4.
GM Cannons, 20.</i>

00:32:48.340 --> 00:32:51.670
<i>Balls, 12.
Supply containers, 40.</i>

00:32:51.840 --> 00:32:54.470
<i>40 relief pilots have also arrived.</i>

00:32:55.010 --> 00:32:57.010
We appreciate the fresh pilots.

00:32:57.850 --> 00:33:00.180
I guess this was
the little girl's breaking point.

00:33:00.310 --> 00:33:01.350
Yes, sir.

00:33:17.660 --> 00:33:24.210
<i>Now pressurizing decks.
New pilots, report to briefing room.</i>

00:33:25.330 --> 00:33:28.500
<i>Deck 4, mobile suit berthing
operations complete.</i>

00:33:29.000 --> 00:33:31.050
<i>Begin closing gate!</i>

00:33:31.300 --> 00:33:32.550
<i>Check all safeties!</i>

00:33:32.630 --> 00:33:35.680
<i>- Begin securing mobile suits to hangar.</i>

00:33:35.680 --> 00:33:36.390
- Hang on, they're all kids!

00:33:36.390 --> 00:33:37.890
<i>- Begin supplying and inspections.</i>

00:33:37.970 --> 00:33:39.390
A Gundam!

00:33:40.390 --> 00:33:41.890
It's a Gundam!

00:33:43.850 --> 00:33:45.140
What the--?

00:33:52.280 --> 00:33:56.200
They're your men.
Take good care of them, Commander lo.

00:33:56.280 --> 00:33:58.370
What a sick joke.

00:33:59.780 --> 00:34:01.910
Little patriots, huh?

00:34:02.040 --> 00:34:05.580
This explains why the Federation is
sending out multiple Gundam prototypes.

00:34:06.370 --> 00:34:10.090
- Hey! Captain!
- Ensign, please!

00:34:10.210 --> 00:34:12.210
Screw you! Get lost!

00:34:17.340 --> 00:34:19.350
Hey! Claudia!

00:34:20.890 --> 00:34:23.930
Wake up! Claudia!

00:34:24.310 --> 00:34:25.940
Wait, are you--

00:34:26.440 --> 00:34:28.270
You're an officer, damn it!

00:34:29.770 --> 00:34:31.770
What the hell are you thinking?!

00:34:32.110 --> 00:34:34.900
- How long have you been using?!
- Ow! You're hurting me!

00:34:36.110 --> 00:34:36.950
Now I...

00:34:38.280 --> 00:34:42.700
Now I understand how your father felt!

00:34:44.830 --> 00:34:46.750
When he was ground down

00:34:46.910 --> 00:34:50.790
by the reality that he let hundreds
of millions of Moore citizens die!

00:34:52.550 --> 00:34:55.590
Lo, you don't know what it's like.

00:34:56.340 --> 00:35:00.050
I'm going to order more
people to their deaths!

00:35:00.640 --> 00:35:03.470
Even those children who were
sent here like expendable goods!

00:35:04.390 --> 00:35:08.810
You should be feeling
this same pain, too!

00:35:14.230 --> 00:35:16.320
- That's amazing!
- That's our ace sniper!

00:35:16.400 --> 00:35:18.450
A special two-rank promotion!

00:35:18.530 --> 00:35:20.740
Here's to the Ensign!

00:35:20.820 --> 00:35:22.450
Show us your insignia!

00:35:22.830 --> 00:35:24.740
Just this once.

00:35:26.950 --> 00:35:28.460
That's so cool!

00:35:29.580 --> 00:35:31.040
Want a belt, Ensign?

00:35:37.800 --> 00:35:42.010
I didn't mean to...
Sorry.

00:35:42.640 --> 00:35:44.350
Don't mind me...

00:35:45.470 --> 00:35:49.350
Don't be like that.
Are you guys all weepy drunks?

00:35:49.850 --> 00:35:52.690
Thanks for throwing
this party for me.

00:35:53.810 --> 00:35:57.070
I'm okay with it, don't worry.
It was an order.

00:35:57.820 --> 00:36:00.450
And I want to protect my fleetmates.

00:36:01.240 --> 00:36:04.830
In fact, it was an honor to be asked.

00:36:12.000 --> 00:36:15.170
These pictures sure take me back.

00:36:16.210 --> 00:36:19.380
I remember the Colony Air Race
like it was yesterday.

00:36:20.800 --> 00:36:23.390
That was such a huge win.

00:36:24.140 --> 00:36:29.560
We did everything ourselves, didn't we?
From the planning to the sponsor hunting.

00:36:31.770 --> 00:36:35.650
I thought that we could
do everything ourselves.

00:36:37.230 --> 00:36:41.150
I still see those days in my dreams.

00:36:41.360 --> 00:36:43.570
Drugs can't take you back.

00:36:44.660 --> 00:36:47.660
Lo doesn't actually enjoy war.

00:36:48.040 --> 00:36:51.210
He's just the type of person
who only feels alive

00:36:51.290 --> 00:36:54.670
when he pushes himself to the limit.

00:36:55.330 --> 00:36:59.880
He can only live
in the madness of war.

00:37:00.760 --> 00:37:02.880
I feel sorry for him.

00:37:10.930 --> 00:37:12.730
Ensign Daryl!

00:37:12.810 --> 00:37:14.020
We'll be heading out first.

00:37:35.540 --> 00:37:38.170
My father is a historian.

00:37:39.250 --> 00:37:42.470
He's in prison right now
as a dissident.

00:37:43.880 --> 00:37:48.890
The military said he'd be spared if I helped
the war effort with my research.

00:37:50.060 --> 00:37:52.430
My father was the sort of man
who kept on fighting

00:37:52.560 --> 00:37:57.310
even after many attempts on
his life and losing his left hand,

00:37:58.230 --> 00:38:03.240
but I did as I was told
and cut off your right arm.

00:38:05.650 --> 00:38:08.820
Out of ego and self-preservation.

00:38:08.950 --> 00:38:10.410
Let's survive this.

00:38:12.870 --> 00:38:16.330
Let's survive and laugh from
the bottom of our hearts someday.

00:38:18.500 --> 00:38:23.420
This irrational reality is the real enemy
that's making us suffer.

00:38:25.010 --> 00:38:29.010
Those of us who live in times of war
undergo lots of little ordeals,

00:38:29.680 --> 00:38:33.020
and maybe it's a miracle
just to survive in this war,

00:38:34.350 --> 00:38:39.690
but I'm sure that there are miracles
even in lives as dark as ours.

00:38:50.370 --> 00:38:54.370
I want to laugh from
the bottom of my heart.

00:39:14.600 --> 00:39:16.730
<i>- Ensign Daryl.
- Yes, sir.</i>

00:39:16.980 --> 00:39:19.730
<i>Everything hinges on your success.</i>

00:39:20.020 --> 00:39:23.190
<i>I apologize for being unable to salute,
but roger that, sir.</i>

00:39:23.610 --> 00:39:25.230
We're all counting on you.

00:39:34.030 --> 00:39:36.200
Daryl Lorenz, launching.

00:39:48.260 --> 00:39:51.010
Move closer!
Closer, closer!

00:39:51.930 --> 00:39:56.770
Our mobile suit force will begin
the operation at 2400 hours.

00:39:57.350 --> 00:39:59.440
Act as my shield.

00:39:59.770 --> 00:40:02.940
I'll be avoiding
any random skirmishes en route.

00:40:03.690 --> 00:40:06.320
The Full Armor Gundam's sole mission

00:40:06.400 --> 00:40:10.910
is to destroy the enemy fleet and
eliminate the enemy's ace sniper.

00:40:12.160 --> 00:40:16.290
This is a messed-up world where
someone who kills lots of people

00:40:16.410 --> 00:40:18.290
gets praised as a hero.

00:40:18.830 --> 00:40:22.290
An endless loop of
planning ops and fighting.

00:40:22.420 --> 00:40:26.920
Even if the players change,
the mission we call war continues.

00:40:27.250 --> 00:40:30.590
Try to ignore it all you want,
but there's no escaping it.

00:40:31.880 --> 00:40:34.300
I love mobile suits.

00:40:34.430 --> 00:40:38.310
I'm hopelessly in love with
these machines that amplify my abilities.

00:40:38.430 --> 00:40:40.390
It gets me fired up from head to toe.

00:40:41.350 --> 00:40:45.480
Call it bad karma
or sinful or whatever,

00:40:46.020 --> 00:40:48.730
but I'll break free of anything
that ties me down

00:40:49.150 --> 00:40:52.910
and keep fighting to the brink of hell itself.

00:40:53.740 --> 00:40:57.950
Farewell, my brother and sister
fellow expendables.

00:40:58.370 --> 00:41:01.160
If any of us survive, I'm buying.

00:41:07.000 --> 00:41:08.090
This is lo Fleming.

00:41:08.460 --> 00:41:10.920
Full Armor Gundam, launching!

00:41:22.310 --> 00:41:24.690
All you innocent children...

00:41:25.310 --> 00:41:27.360
Please, come back safely.

00:41:27.480 --> 00:41:29.530
As many as possible.

00:41:36.820 --> 00:41:40.160
Damn, they're like tidy candles
on a birthday cake out there.

00:41:40.740 --> 00:41:43.160
But they just have numbers...

00:41:48.880 --> 00:41:50.880
- Philip!
- Where is he?!

00:41:51.090 --> 00:41:53.380
- <i>Hold fire! Hold fire!
- People have</i> been hit!

00:41:53.510 --> 00:41:57.340
We can't win with uncoordinated fire!
We'll be wiped out like this!

00:41:59.180 --> 00:42:00.310
Okay, then...

00:42:01.810 --> 00:42:04.230
If I can keep their formation split up...

00:42:06.770 --> 00:42:09.060
...this'll be easier than slicing
a cake with a knife.

00:42:09.860 --> 00:42:13.240
<i>We have to do it like in training!
Link up with each other!</i>

00:42:13.400 --> 00:42:15.990
- Crap, we lost another!
- Shut up! Don't break forma--

00:42:16.570 --> 00:42:17.530
Chief!

00:42:17.870 --> 00:42:20.580
Crap, they've started forming up again!

00:42:21.200 --> 00:42:26.830
Man, it's been forever since the last time
I had a slice of Grandma's apple tart.

00:42:36.090 --> 00:42:37.760
<i>We got him... We got him!</i>

00:42:41.180 --> 00:42:43.100
I'll be joining you soon!

00:42:54.110 --> 00:42:57.240
Now on penetration route.
Everything going according to plan.

00:42:57.700 --> 00:43:01.620
Target acquired. Take it from here,
Petty Officer Layton.

00:43:01.870 --> 00:43:02.870
Roger that.

00:43:08.580 --> 00:43:10.210
Gotta wait 200 seconds...

00:43:10.540 --> 00:43:12.630
Keep it together, Layton!

00:43:13.130 --> 00:43:14.420
Prof. Karla!

00:43:14.710 --> 00:43:17.590
Are you planning to go down with this ship?

00:43:18.260 --> 00:43:20.220
Thanks to my work with that weapon,

00:43:20.340 --> 00:43:24.100
I've learned how the world works
and realized what a fool I am.

00:43:24.180 --> 00:43:25.930
Thank you, Sexton.

00:43:26.060 --> 00:43:29.650
We should escape! If we bring your research
back to the homeland, Zeon can--

00:43:29.770 --> 00:43:31.610
Escape by yourself.

00:43:31.690 --> 00:43:34.980
The device is complete.
You don't have to babysit me anymore, right?

00:43:35.150 --> 00:43:36.610
No, but--

00:43:37.780 --> 00:43:38.990
The data!

00:43:42.160 --> 00:43:43.330
Professor!

00:43:43.870 --> 00:43:46.660
I don't believe it...
Fine, have it your way!

00:43:58.090 --> 00:43:59.260
<i>Professor!</i>

00:43:59.380 --> 00:44:03.350
<i>Relax! Do it like in your military
training and you'll be fine!</i>

00:44:14.230 --> 00:44:15.860
<i>It's the Gundam!</i>

00:44:23.870 --> 00:44:26.370
Damn you, Gundam!

00:44:43.680 --> 00:44:44.390
It's time!

00:44:52.020 --> 00:44:54.350
I did it!
I did it, Ensign!

00:44:54.440 --> 00:44:56.190
I did it! I did--

00:45:57.080 --> 00:45:58.960
Engineering hit!

00:45:59.170 --> 00:46:00.750
Give me a damage report!

00:46:01.340 --> 00:46:04.090
We can't afford to go down here--

00:46:15.730 --> 00:46:18.060
Load the wounded into the pods first!

00:46:18.150 --> 00:46:20.230
This one is packed, too...

00:46:20.520 --> 00:46:22.400
- This man's injured!
- Give us a hand!

00:46:22.820 --> 00:46:25.110
- Hey, are you all right?
- Let's get him into a pod!

00:46:25.200 --> 00:46:26.150
Right.

00:46:39.500 --> 00:46:40.670
Graham!

00:46:41.880 --> 00:46:44.420
XO Graham, are you all right?

00:46:48.140 --> 00:46:49.680
Get your hands off me.

00:46:50.220 --> 00:46:53.970
The ship's about to go up.
I've given the order to abandon ship.

00:46:54.060 --> 00:46:55.680
You did what?

00:46:56.600 --> 00:46:58.310
You're abandoning ship?!

00:47:00.310 --> 00:47:05.650
You incompetent elites... First you cost us
our homeland, and now our fleet!

00:47:06.700 --> 00:47:11.200
You think I can look my late wife
and daughter in the eye if I run?

00:47:11.370 --> 00:47:12.660
Graham...

00:47:13.410 --> 00:47:15.750
For the honor of Moore.

00:47:20.750 --> 00:47:22.790
I'll be joining you.

00:47:46.900 --> 00:47:48.740
Claudia?

00:47:50.530 --> 00:47:52.070
Hey, what was that light?

00:47:52.160 --> 00:47:53.910
That blast was huge!

00:47:53.990 --> 00:47:56.410
That wasn't our mothership, was it?

00:47:58.120 --> 00:48:00.750
The battle's not over yet.

00:48:00.920 --> 00:48:04.170
There's still a powerful enemy in there.

00:48:04.710 --> 00:48:07.590
He wasn't in this combat zone.

00:48:10.220 --> 00:48:12.260
It's you, isn't it?

00:48:51.800 --> 00:48:53.470
<i>We've received intel that
the Living Dead Division's battle</i>

00:48:53.590 --> 00:48:56.050
<i>has spread from Banchi 3
to Banchi 2.</i>

00:48:56.180 --> 00:48:58.390
<i>- Tell all the reinforcements!
- Roger that!</i>

00:49:06.770 --> 00:49:09.150
Daryl... Guys...

00:49:09.440 --> 00:49:12.950
Hold out until these reinforcements arrive.

00:50:36.280 --> 00:50:39.070
Damn it, die already!

00:50:46.250 --> 00:50:50.000
Karla, this is amazing!
This mobile suit you built for me

00:50:50.670 --> 00:50:54.170
is way better than
the arms and legs I lost!

00:50:55.510 --> 00:50:59.430
The enemy flagship is dead in space
from a friendly mobile suit force attack.

00:50:59.550 --> 00:51:02.260
Multiple Zeon troops
are still alive inside.

00:51:02.430 --> 00:51:04.390
We are en route to board
and take the enemy ship.

00:51:04.930 --> 00:51:06.180
Take the ship?

00:51:06.270 --> 00:51:09.600
This lifeboat doesn't have enough oxygen.

00:51:11.190 --> 00:51:13.780
<i>Chief Petty Officer Chiba
will take point in a Ball.</i>

00:51:21.370 --> 00:51:24.790
- Cornelius, you ever shoot anyone?
- No.

00:51:25.700 --> 00:51:29.790
I finally understand why he wants
to listen to music in battle.

00:52:31.140 --> 00:52:34.150
I can do this...
I can take him!

00:52:42.530 --> 00:52:46.530
The engine room's that way.
Take your men and secure Engineering.

00:52:46.660 --> 00:52:50.040
- But we're just mechanics...
- You've had training!

00:52:50.790 --> 00:52:52.040
Roger that.

00:53:07.890 --> 00:53:09.140
There's air.

00:53:09.220 --> 00:53:12.060
They must be up where
this music is coming from.

00:53:24.200 --> 00:53:26.410
Thank you, Prof. Karla.

00:53:26.570 --> 00:53:29.740
This explosion should spread
through the entire ship.

00:53:29.870 --> 00:53:33.920
Let's take them all with us
and put an end to this nightmare.

00:53:34.830 --> 00:53:37.250
Freeze! All of you,
stay where you are!

00:53:37.340 --> 00:53:41.260
We're the Earth Federation Forces
Moore Brotherhood!

00:53:41.340 --> 00:53:44.840
This ship is under our control!
Surrender yourselves peacefully!

00:53:44.930 --> 00:53:46.590
Is the person in charge here?

00:53:47.300 --> 00:53:49.430
Who's the ranking officer?!

00:53:57.150 --> 00:54:00.610
No Zeon soldier would live with
the disgrace of being taken prisoner.

00:54:00.690 --> 00:54:04.280
He's right! It's a matter of
a soldier's honor and pride! Never!

00:54:07.160 --> 00:54:09.580
Die, Gundam!

00:54:10.660 --> 00:54:14.910
Daryl, I won't let you die alone.

00:54:15.000 --> 00:54:15.870
I'll join you.

00:54:17.460 --> 00:54:19.130
This Will kill you!

00:54:25.340 --> 00:54:26.800
Let's do this.

00:54:27.220 --> 00:54:28.720
- Sieg--
- Wait!

00:54:43.030 --> 00:54:48.320
This has to end! How long is the hatred
and killing going to go on?

00:54:48.740 --> 00:54:52.660
It has to end.
This... has to end.

00:54:55.370 --> 00:54:58.580
All of you, come here!
Get a move on!

00:54:58.670 --> 00:55:00.630
Why hasn't there been an explosion?

00:55:00.710 --> 00:55:04.840
Maybe they failed...
Plan B. Switch to Plan B.

00:55:04.960 --> 00:55:07.300
Blowing yourselves up is pointless!
This has to stop.

00:55:07.380 --> 00:55:10.850
We won't be taken prisoner!
We'll take you out with us!

00:55:10.970 --> 00:55:14.680
- You took our families and loved ones!
- You'll feel our hatred!

00:55:15.230 --> 00:55:18.350
We've endured plenty of suffering ourselves!

00:55:18.440 --> 00:55:21.770
This sector is where
our colonies used to be!

00:55:21.860 --> 00:55:23.860
It's where our homeland was!

00:55:23.980 --> 00:55:26.440
- Homeland?
- They're from Side 4?

00:55:26.820 --> 00:55:31.370
That's right. Our home was taken,
our mothership was destroyed,

00:55:31.450 --> 00:55:33.540
and now there's only
a handful of us left!

00:55:33.870 --> 00:55:36.540
I don't want to see
any more of us die!

00:55:36.870 --> 00:55:39.460
Let's figure out a way
to survive this together!

00:55:39.540 --> 00:55:42.040
Fighting until we're both wiped out

00:55:42.340 --> 00:55:43.800
is just stupid!

00:55:45.590 --> 00:55:47.220
What are you--

00:56:11.660 --> 00:56:14.330
- It worked!
- It was a longshot, but it worked!

00:56:30.340 --> 00:56:32.090
This thing's built tough, all right.

00:56:32.260 --> 00:56:34.850
If I ditch the extra armor,
I can still fight!

00:56:45.320 --> 00:56:48.740
I'm gonna put an end to this.
I'll kill him.

00:56:58.910 --> 00:57:01.620
Hurry up!
We can't hold them off!

00:57:03.750 --> 00:57:04.380
Whoa!

00:57:06.750 --> 00:57:08.460
Sieg Zeon!

00:57:11.420 --> 00:57:14.140
Oh, come on! Not after we made it
all the way to the magazine!

00:58:02.520 --> 00:58:05.810
When you hear my jazz,
that's when you die!

00:58:06.690 --> 00:58:08.940
Peglegs!

00:59:00.530 --> 00:59:03.700
Why?! Why can't I beat him?!

00:59:05.290 --> 00:59:06.910
I get it now, Karla.

00:59:07.830 --> 00:59:11.880
When I met you,
that was my miracle.

01:00:02.140 --> 01:00:03.640
No way!

01:00:03.760 --> 01:00:08.600
He's missing all his limbs?
I lost to a guy like this?!

01:01:13.620 --> 01:01:16.960
I see. Claudia isn't with you?

01:01:17.210 --> 01:01:20.670
She was the ship's captain,
so she probably...

01:01:35.560 --> 01:01:38.900
Thanks. The reinforcements
you brought saved us, Fisher.

01:01:39.230 --> 01:01:42.400
No, I just did it without thinking.

01:01:42.700 --> 01:01:46.660
We lost the Psycho Zaku, though.

01:01:47.070 --> 01:01:48.660
How do we report this?

01:01:49.580 --> 01:01:54.000
When Prof. Karla recovers,
the Reuse Psycho Device will be mass-produced.

01:01:54.500 --> 01:01:58.710
More pilots will probably decide
to take on the same fate as you.

01:01:59.000 --> 01:02:04.510
Yeah, the Reuse Psycho Device can turn
even average pilots into supermen.

01:02:05.970 --> 01:02:10.930
They only have to cut off their limbs.
Just like I did.

01:02:12.480 --> 01:02:17.100
That's enough, Living Dead Division!
Torture is a treaty violation!

01:02:17.230 --> 01:02:20.610
As a Special Service member,
I can no longer turn a blind eye.

01:02:21.480 --> 01:02:24.900
We understand, sir.
Our apologies.

01:02:25.780 --> 01:02:30.910
Go ahead. You have five minutes.
Audio and video will be recorded.

01:02:31.330 --> 01:02:33.040
Thank you.

01:02:35.460 --> 01:02:37.420
Lo Fleming...

01:02:37.710 --> 01:02:40.460
Son of the former leader of Side 4.

01:02:40.630 --> 01:02:43.420
Attached to the Earth Federation Forces'
Moore Brotherhood.

01:02:43.550 --> 01:02:48.140
And notorious Gundam pilot.

01:02:51.260 --> 01:02:54.270
Daryl Lorenz...

01:02:54.350 --> 01:02:58.980
C'mon, tell me.
How do you pilot a mobile suit

01:02:59.110 --> 01:03:01.820
with that pathetic,
crippled body of yours?

01:03:04.650 --> 01:03:07.660
I wanted to put an end
to this by killing you.

01:03:08.240 --> 01:03:10.490
I thought if I could defeat the Gundam,

01:03:10.620 --> 01:03:13.620
it would set me free from
the nightmare of war.

01:03:13.830 --> 01:03:15.660
Nightmare?

01:03:17.830 --> 01:03:20.330
You're playing the victim
after all you've done?

01:03:20.420 --> 01:03:22.960
You beat my Gundam with
power you gained

01:03:23.090 --> 01:03:25.840
by offering up your body
to your mobile suit.

01:03:25.920 --> 01:03:27.840
Helluva rush, isn't it?

01:03:28.010 --> 01:03:32.970
Even as we curse war, we become
more and more obsessed with it.

01:03:35.180 --> 01:03:39.350
It's our fate to go on fighting.

01:03:45.030 --> 01:03:49.660
This war isn't going to end just yet.

01:08:53.580 --> 01:08:55.500
Translation, Adaptation and Subtitling:
David Fleming
